   "title": "The Miners' Hall",
   "text": "Halls like this were built by the miners themselves, a few pence a week from every pay packet. They held a library, a stage, a billiard table and, on a good night, a choir and a quarrel. When the pits closed many were shut, sold or left to rot. This one was lent back to the valley."
